This project builds upon and depends on several open-source projects.
Their licenses are included here as required.

LIBERO — Benchmark and Task Definitions
----------------------------------------
License: MIT License (code), CC BY 4.0 (datasets)
Copyright (c) 2023 Lifelong Robot Learning
Source: https://github.com/Lifelong-Robot-Learning/LIBERO
Citation: Wang et al., "LIBERO: Lifelong Robot Learning", ICLR 2024.

  The 131 task XML files in libero_mjx/assets/xml/ are derived from
  LIBERO's robosuite task definitions. They reference (but do not
  embed) 3D models, textures, and mesh assets that remain in the
  LIBERO and robosuite packages. Demonstration datasets used for BC
  training are licensed under Creative Commons Attribution 4.0
  International (CC BY 4.0).

  MIT License — LIBERO

  Copyright (c) 2023 Lifelong Robot Learning

  Permission is hereby granted, free of charge, to any person obtaining a copy
  of this software and associated documentation files (the "Software"), to deal
  in the Software without restriction, including without limitation the rights
  to use, copy, modify, merge, publish, distribute, sublicense, and/or sell
  copies of the Software, and to permit persons to whom the Software is
  furnished to do so, subject to the following conditions:

  The above copyright notice and this permission notice shall be included in all
  copies or substantial portions of the Software.

robosuite — Robot Simulation Framework
---------------------------------------
License: MIT License
Copyright (c) 2022 Stanford Vision and Learning Lab and UT Robot Perception
and Learning Lab
Source: https://github.com/ARISE-Initiative/robosuite

  The OSC (Operational Space) controller in libero_mjx/controllers/osc.py
  and libero_mjx/warp_env.py is a port of robosuite's OSC_POSE controller.
  Robot models (Franka Panda) and scene assets are referenced by path
  from the robosuite package and are not redistributed in this repository.

  MIT License — robosuite

  Copyright (c) 2022 Stanford Vision and Learning Lab and UT Robot Perception
  and Learning Lab

  Permission is hereby granted, free of charge, to any person obtaining a copy
  of this software and associated documentation files (the "Software"), to deal
  in the Software without restriction, including without limitation the rights
  to use, copy, modify, merge, publish, distribute, sublicense, and/or sell
  copies of the Software, and to permit persons to whom the Software is
  furnished to do so, subject to the following conditions:

  The above copyright notice and this permission notice shall be included in all
  copies or substantial portions of the Software.

MuJoCo & MuJoCo Warp — Physics Simulator
-----------------------------------------
License: Apache License, Version 2.0
Copyright Google DeepMind
Source: https://github.com/google-deepmind/mujoco
        https://github.com/google-deepmind/mujoco_warp

  This project depends on MuJoCo, MuJoCo MJX, and MuJoCo Warp for
  GPU-parallel physics simulation. No MuJoCo source code is
  redistributed in this repository.

  Licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0 (the "License");
  you may not use this file except in compliance with the License.
  You may obtain a copy of the License at:

      http://www.apache.org/licenses/LICENSE-2.0

robomimic — Robot Learning from Demonstration
---------------------------------------------
License: MIT License
Copyright (c) ARISE Initiative
Source: https://github.com/ARISE-Initiative/robomimic

  The BC transformer policy architecture follows robomimic's design
  patterns. robomimic is used as a dependency via the LIBERO package.

